Ekkyklema · Projection on White Model (15 s sample)

Made entirely in code: no generated images, no stock footage, no photographs. The model is the motion build's
reconstruction (../motion), restyled; every light, colour, label and line is drawn by the page (three.js + 2D canvas).

STYLE AND TECHNIQUE
- Lemo-Opuscar, "Projection on White Model" style (styles/white-model/STYLE.md), DIRECTOR.md and TECHNIQUE.md,
  by LemoLab. https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar — code MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 LemoLab), content CC BY 4.0.
  Adapted, not copied: the projection-as-light term, the readout / pin / range-line grammar, the house-light / relay /
  lamp-strike sequence and the sound palette. What was taken, and how it changed, is listed in README.md.
- Tools used from the library, unmodified: core/audio/sfx.py, core/audio/sampler.py, core/render/mux.sh,
  core/render/sheet.py (MIT).

SAMPLES (sound)
- Versilian Community Sample Library (VCSL), Versilian Studios — CC0 1.0. Bowed vibraphone, vibraphone, glockenspiel,
  marimba, hand chimes, tubular bells. Fetched with lemo-opuscar's tools/fetch.sh instruments vcsl.
- All other sounds (room tone, projector fan, relays, lamp strike, door creak, wheel rumble, ticks) are synthesised.

FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1, licence texts in fonts/)
